Done. `integration-landscape.json` written and validated against the pipeline's STAGE 6 consumer logic.

## Verdict: `HAS_INTEGRATIONS` — but only just

Colombia has **exactly one** genuine system-to-system statutory channel. 3 of 4 authority channels and 5 of 6 in-scope filings are manual.

| Authority | Integration | Channel | Directions |
|---|---|---|---|
| **DIAN-NE** | **yes** | SOAP 1.2 `SendNominaSync` | outbound + inbound |
| DIAN-MUISCA | no | portal round-trip (IFE) | outbound |
| PILA-OI | no | private-operator portal upload | outbound + inbound |
| FONDOS-CESANTIAS | no | private-operator portal upload | outbound + inbound |

**Live-verified, not inferred.** Both WSDLs returned HTTP 200 unauthenticated and both declare `wsdl:operation name="SendNominaSync"` — production (`vpfe.dian.gov.co`, 61,719 bytes) and habilitación (`vpfe-hab.dian.gov.co`, 61,727 bytes). The DIAN toolkit ZIP downloaded at 5,528,509 bytes containing XSD **v1.0.6** for both `NominaIndividual` and `NominaIndividualDeAjuste`, the UBL 2.1/XAdES schema set, two sample XMLs and the 269-page annex. DIAN-NE is **BUILD-READY with zero artefact gaps** — no login, no certificate, no CAPTCHA anywhere in the artefact path. I did not call the live service endpoints.

**The judgement call you should look at.** ARUS/Enlace Operativo markets "APIS PILA" and runs a developer portal at `suaporte.com.co/portal-apis/`. I fetched it — it renders a welcome shell with no catalogue, no endpoints, no OpenAPI/WSDL. So it is a *private commercial* offering from one intermediary of seven, with no public spec and no statutory standing. I scored PILA `integration: false` and recorded the finding in a `commercial_api_caveat` field rather than dropping it. Marking it true would have generated a runbook nobody can build. It is worth revisiting only once the client's operator is fixed.

**Three things worth flagging:**

1. **The agent definition file does not exist.** `.claude/agents/si-discovery.md` is absent, as is `shared/si-runbook/` (and `si_scope_check.py`). I reconstructed the schema from the only authoritative consumer — STAGE 6 of `mercans_pipeline_v2_9.sh`, which reads top-level `verdict` and iterates `authorities` on `integration is True` + non-empty `code`, plus the five fields its index prompt requires. Recorded in `_schema_note`. **STAGE 6b will also fail to run its scope check** until `shared/si-runbook` is installed.

2. **I split DIAN into two rows.** One legal entity, two irreconcilable postures — the payroll web service is M2M, while F350/F220/2276 are portal round-trips gated by the IFE, a signature instrument bound to a *natural person* and exercised interactively. That is the structural reason no M2M exists there. A single DIAN yes/no would have been misleading.

3. **A defect in DIAN's own annex.** Section 9.7 bullets `Metodo: SendBillSync` while the surrounding prose, the request envelope and both WSDLs say `SendNominaSync`. The WSDL is authoritative; noted so the runbook stage doesn't inherit the error.

No runbooks written, as instructed. Next stage will branch to the runbook path and create `03-statutory-integrations/DIAN-NE/`.

